{
  "slug": "raffle",
  "title": "Raffle: a fixed four-entrant commit-reveal draw",
  "kind": "coin_puzzle",
  "security_scope": "Original WIP teaching policy for issue #11, not ready for real funds. A raffle coin holding exactly 4,000 mojos (four 1,000-mojo tickets) curries one proper list: the ordered-payout module hash and four entrants, each (payout puzzle hash, sha256(commit domain || 32-byte salt)). Before the coin is ten blocks old, anyone may draw by revealing all four salts; the seed hashes them in roster order and the winner is seed[31] % 4 (unbiased because four divides 256), receiving the whole pot. At or after ten blocks, anyone may refund: the pot moves into an ordered-payout queue that repays each entrant one ticket. Draw and refund are mutually exclusive in time. The puzzle only emits conditions; consensus enforces ages and amounts.",
  "environment": "strict",
  "reference_mode": "module",
  "provenance": {
    "classification": "original teaching implementation",
    "references": [
      "https://chialisp.com/conditions/",
      "https://chialisp.com/chialisp-currying/",
      "https://github.com/judeallred/chialisp-oxide/issues/11"
    ],
    "source_origin": "All four paired source files (Rust export, independent Chialisp reference, Rue port and Python oracle) are original implementations of this explicit teaching contract. The refund path composes the repository's own ordered-payout export; no published raffle is copied or ported.",
    "limitations": [
      "Withholding: salts are revealed together in one draw spend, so whoever assembles them learns the outcome first and can withhold, forcing a refund. That cannot steer the winner, but it lets a would-be loser cancel the raffle at no cost; there is no forfeit or penalty.",
      "Each entrant must keep their salt secret until the draw and choose it unpredictably; the chain checks its width, not its entropy. Fixture salts are public test data.",
      "The roster is fixed at creation, so there is no late or double entry, but the host must check before funding that the four payout hashes are distinct, the pot is exactly 4,000 mojos, and the module field names the selected ordered-payout artifact.",
      "SHA-256 is an assumption; proof models do not cover SHA, this export or the refund queue. The draw is not unbiasable beyond what these finite vectors and simulator runs show."
    ]
  },
